<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:50:18 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Elon Musk and Donald Trump: What their growing ties mean for Ukraine</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-elon-musk-and-donald-trump-what-their-growing-ties-mean-for-ukraine</link><description>
The recent disruption of SpaceX’s Starlink satellite internet service in Ukraine comes as Washington steps up pressure on Kyiv to halt its strikes on Russian oil refineries. The system plays a key role in Ukraine’s long-range drone operations, raising questions about the implications of the disruption and Elon Musk’s increasingly close ties with Donald Trump.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9579dc0a-c894-11f1-a670-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-140816-140948-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9579dc0a-c894-11f1-a670-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-140816-140948-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9a36d00e-c894-11f1-a3e5-c3f8d9655db0</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:39:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Chad’s ICC exit plans raise concerns over Sudan war crimes probes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-chad-s-icc-exit-plans-raise-concerns-over-sudan-war-crimes-probes</link><description>
Last July, Chad announced plans to withdraw from the International Criminal Court, accusing it of inefficiency and of disproportionately targeting African nations. The decision could complicate future investigations into alleged war crimes linked to the conflict in neighbouring Sudan, particularly as ICC investigators engage with Sudanese refugees sheltering in eastern Chad. Despite the political headwinds, humanitarian organisations remain on the ground, supporting those displaced by the crisis, as FRANCE 24’s Harold Girard reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bd3a560c-c885-11f1-b326-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-214752-215020-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bd3a560c-c885-11f1-b326-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-214752-215020-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c23043ba-c885-11f1-a147-9310c30c2b14</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:36:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine's Zelensky defies Trump with Russian refinery strikes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-ukraine-s-zelensky-defies-trump-with-russian-refinery-strikes</link><description>
Ukraine will no longer abide by US President Donald Trump's demands not to strike Russian oil refineries, President Volodymyr Zelensky said in remarks published Thursday, amid deepening tensions between the two leaders over a US-Russia diesel agreement. Relations between Kyiv and Washington have soured since last week, when Trump eased sanctions on Russia in exchange for Moscow releasing large amounts of diesel onto global markets. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Angela Diffley tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0ac182bc-c893-11f1-b311-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-133345-133853-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0ac182bc-c893-11f1-b311-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-133345-133853-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0fb4d90e-c893-11f1-b041-71a412ed6201</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:34:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Outcry over US plans to livestream firing squad execution of Fort Hood shooter</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-outcry-over-us-plans-to-livestream-firing-squad-execution-of-fort-hood-shooter</link><description>
US Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth last week announced plans to livestream the firing squad execution of Fort Hood shooter Nidal Hasan, triggering a backlash among Republicans in Congress, religious leaders and international observers. The event would be extraordinary, even for a country that has long employed capital punishment. A government execution has never been broadcast or livestreamed, according to death penalty experts, and the US military ​has not executed anyone by firing squad since 1945. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5a9dc4a4-c892-11f1-95c2-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-131055-131541-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5a9dc4a4-c892-11f1-95c2-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-131055-131541-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5fded41c-c892-11f1-9661-2d57375c8d74</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:33:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Business</category><title>China, North Korea open long-delayed trade bridge</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261015-china-north-korea-open-long-delayed-trade-bridge</link><description>
China and North Korea formally opened the Yalu River Bridge on Thursday, connecting Dandong in China with Sinuiju in North Korea. Beijing says the bridge will promote economic and trade cooperation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d479a1a-c892-11f1-b7e4-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-333e0e64.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d479a1a-c892-11f1-b7e4-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-333e0e64.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7b971daa-c88c-11f1-b310-0f63de7da4af</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:20:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Charlotte Lam</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Observers</category><title>A deep dive into the global spy plane market</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261015-deep-dive-global-spy-plane-market</link><description>
All over the globe – from the Mexican border to Syria to the Sahel – companies are renting out planes equipped with powerful sensors to armies and intelligence services for political missions. The market may be discreet, but it isn’t invisible.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aa880524-c7cf-11f1-886f-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/image-collee-1-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aa880524-c7cf-11f1-886f-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/image-collee-1-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">05653f7a-c7d0-11f1-abf8-f59ce405ed29</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:09:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Macron's 'trickle-down economics': French poverty at 'highest level' in decades, hunger on the rise</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/macron-s-trickle-down-economics-french-poverty-at-highest-level-in-decades-hunger-on-the-rise</link><description>
Charles Pellegrin is pleased to welcome Nicolas Vercken, Director of Advocacy for Oxfam France. France’s tax inequality is under scrutiny and Oxfam is challenging the state over its constitutional obligations. “It’s not so much about how much the percentage of tax and the burden of our tax system, it’s who you tax and for what,” explains Vercken. As France confronts mounting fiscal pressures and contentious budget negotiations, Oxfam France is challenging the constitutional foundations of the country's tax system, arguing that successive fiscal reforms have disproportionately benefited the wealthiest while exacerbating economic inequality. Their legal initiative seeks to establish whether the French state has failed in its constitutional obligations, potentially placing fiscal inequality under judicial scrutiny for years to come.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3cfb6e4a-c7e0-11f1-aac6-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-081015-081909-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3cfb6e4a-c7e0-11f1-aac6-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-081015-081909-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">43d1a310-c7e0-11f1-b463-35b540327c3c</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:40:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia detains independent outlet Novaya Gazeta editor Sergei Sokolov</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-russia-detains-novaya-gazeta-editor-in-chief-sergei-sokolov-after-home-search</link><description>
Sergei Sokolov, the editor-in-chief of Russia's independent newspaper Novaya Gazeta, was detained and taken for questioning on Thursday after authorities searched his home, the newspaper said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd8c2f0c-c88b-11f1-8592-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3D79KE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd8c2f0c-c88b-11f1-8592-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3D79KE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f0ab8140-c88b-11f1-9849-0fbb85ce41e0</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:39:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd8c2f0c-c88b-11f1-8592-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3D79KE.jpg">© Igor Ivanko, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Starlink in Ukraine: Musk suggests US govt behind any slowdown</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-starlink-in-ukraine-musk-suggests-us-govt-behind-any-slowdown</link><description>
🇺🇦🇺🇸 As Ukraine reports slowdowns in the Starlink system used for battlefield communications and frontline logistics, Elon Musk says that "any limits on speed or usage are decided by the US military and ultimately POTUS."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ebd04c20-c889-11f1-9320-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/Vignette-Ukraine-Starlink-EN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ebd04c20-c889-11f1-9320-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/Vignette-Ukraine-Starlink-EN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9919bd92-c887-11f1-8e30-63d6ee35c070</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:19:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>'American abandonment' threatens Ukraine's civilians in war against Russia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261015-american-abandonment-threatens-ukraine-s-civilians-in-war-against-russia</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, October 15: First, reported Starlink disruptions in Ukraine make the European front pages. Next, US papers go into more detail about the situation. Also, an unusual alliance forms in Germany between far-right and far-left parties. Meanwhile, the winners of the Wildlife Photographer of the Year awards have been announced. Finally, Finland flaunts its smelly islands.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1ee85026-c885-11f1-9705-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5116b1de.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1ee85026-c885-11f1-9705-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5116b1de.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">804e3c42-c865-11f1-bc3e-3114adfafbf4</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:09:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Emily BOYLE</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Kenya reports second Ebola case, family member of first patient</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-kenya-reports-second-ebola-case-family-member-of-first-patient</link><description>
Kenya reported a second case of Ebola on Wednesday, about a week after recording its first ever infection of the viral disease when a Kenyan who had been living in Congo died in a Nairobi hospital ​on October 5. The ‌second patient, a 39-year-old man, is a close family member of the first case and was already ⁠in quarantine when he fell ill on Tuesday, the health ministry said in a statement.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/deac57ec-c883-11f1-b1ed-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-214417-214616-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/deac57ec-c883-11f1-b1ed-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261014-214417-214616-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e38c3174-c883-11f1-9e8d-4bd4f2dab98c</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:39:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Houthis deny targeting holy city of Medina after Saudi Arabia says it intercepted missile</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261015-houthis-deny-targeting-holy-city-medina-after-saudi-arabia-says-intercepted-missile</link><description>
Yemen's Houthis denied carrying out an attack on Saudi Arabia on Thursday, shortly after Riyadh said it had intercepted a missile targeting the region around the holy city of Medina.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68f50d26-c880-11f1-9523-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/000-1SL9CP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68f50d26-c880-11f1-9523-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/000-1SL9CP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7cce943c-c87d-11f1-8d45-fb20c1b501ef</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:24:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68f50d26-c880-11f1-9523-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/000-1SL9CP.jpg">© Majed Al-Charfi, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Paris des arts</category><title>A cultural stroll through Paris with photographer Nikos Aliagas and writer Jean-Paul Enthoven</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/paris-des-arts/20261015-a-cultural-stroll-through-paris-with-photographer-nikos-aliagas-and-writer-jean-paul-enthoven</link><description>
This week in Paris des Arts, Valérie Fayolle hosts Nikos Aliagas, a TV presenter and photographer. He takes us to his exhibit on old age at the Musée de l’Homme.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d2b157b4-c3c7-11f1-af99-c55799ef8309/w:1024/p:16x9/1920x1080-main-PARIS-DES-ARTS-aliagas-enthoven.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d2b157b4-c3c7-11f1-af99-c55799ef8309/w:1024/p:16x9/1920x1080-main-PARIS-DES-ARTS-aliagas-enthoven.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">109e25c2-c867-11f1-857e-71653adee254</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:16:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Valérie FAYOLLE</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French teen charged in school shooting cites revenge for bullying</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261015-france-charges-teen-shooter-citing-revenge-for-bullying-in-school</link><description>
Anti-terrorism prosecutors said a 14-year-old involved in a shooting that wounded teaching staff at a school in the south of France earlier this week was acting out of revenge for bullying. The teenager was charged with attempted murder and remanded in custody Wednesday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5420d744-c881-11f1-9258-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/37dd1f2b82fb621ac1e17c20e2022b63bec92aa7.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5420d744-c881-11f1-9258-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/37dd1f2b82fb621ac1e17c20e2022b63bec92aa7.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">550e24e0-c881-11f1-b7e4-03810c2c482b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:15:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5420d744-c881-11f1-9258-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/37dd1f2b82fb621ac1e17c20e2022b63bec92aa7.jpg">© Miguel Medina, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>EU leaders to clash over long-term budget, Ukraine support</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-eu-leaders-to-clash-over-long-term-budget-ukraine-support</link><description>
European Union leaders ⁠will clash on Thursday ​over the size of bloc's next long-term budget, its sources of revenue and spending priorities, with no immediate deal ​in sight. The budget also covers help for Kyiv. Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky will be joining the meeting on Friday in a bid to rally support amid fresh tension with US President Donald Trump. FRANCE 24's Europe Editor Armen Georgian reports from Brussels, Belgium.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7dd0ea64-c87e-11f1-9b4c-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-110142-110649-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7dd0ea64-c87e-11f1-9b4c-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-110142-110649-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">83020cf2-c87e-11f1-9872-8344ac766569</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:11:14 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>EU leaders head for showdown over bloc long-term budget</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-eu-leaders-head-for-showdown-over-bloc-long-term-budget</link><description>
EU leaders on Thursday head for their biggest clash yet over the bloc's next long-term budget, as they race to lock in a deal before next year's French presidential election. The 27-nation European Union wants an agreement by Christmas, worried that any future dealmaking will be derailed by potential eurosceptic wins in polls taking place across the bloc -- most crucially in key power France. FRANCE 24's Dave Keating reports from Brussels, Belgium.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/693d9a3c-c876-11f1-aef5-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-100212-100701-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/693d9a3c-c876-11f1-aef5-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-100212-100701-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6e83d0b0-c876-11f1-8afd-19f6207f865c</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:09:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Musk suggests US govt behind any slowdown in Ukraine's Starshield system</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-musk-suggests-us-govt-behind-any-slowdown-in-ukraine-s-starshield-system</link><description>
SpaceX boss Elon Musk said Wednesday that any disruptions reported by Ukraine in using the Starshield satellite communications system would be the responsibility of the US government, not his company. "Starshield systems are owned and controlled by the US government. Any limits on speed or usage are decided by the US military and ultimately POTUS," Musk said, referring to US President Donald Trump. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7bd18882-c878-11f1-97f6-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-100832-101418-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7bd18882-c878-11f1-97f6-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-100832-101418-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">80e5bf32-c878-11f1-b6b5-31f1a23838fe</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:08:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Albanian students protest over education, jobs, clash with police</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-albanian-students-protest-over-education-jobs-clash-with-police</link><description>
Demonstrators and riot police clashed in Albania's capital on Wednesday in a second straight day of violence triggered by student protests calling for better university conditions and Prime Minister Edi Rama's resignation. Protesters formed makeshift barricades in the capital, Tirana, while riot police responded with water cannon, after street violence overnight left 16 people arrested and government buildings badly damaged.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e8942f4c-c878-11f1-8c20-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-101448-101622-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e8942f4c-c878-11f1-8c20-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-101448-101622-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">edea0d2c-c878-11f1-b2c4-23804a743c18</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:06:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>China, North Korea open long-delayed border bridge</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-china-north-korea-open-long-delayed-border-bridge</link><description>
China and North Korea officially opened their most significant land border crossing on Thursday, aiming to rejuvenate trade and commerce after years of strained ties and pandemic-related disruptions. Trucks festooned with the national flags of the neighbours drove across the long-delayed 3-km (2-mile) New Yalu River Bridge, its ​towering pylons also ‌decked in flags, linking the Chinese city of Dandong with North Korea. FRANCE 24's Jan Camenzind Broomby reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/336a12b6-c879-11f1-9017-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-101659-101832-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/336a12b6-c879-11f1-9017-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-101659-101832-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3c232686-c879-11f1-a21e-bf194323f93e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:05:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>FRANCE 24 report: India’s Gen Z protesters find gaps in security clampdown</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-france-24-report-india-s-gen-z-protesters-find-gaps-in-security-clampdown</link><description>
India’s capital New Delhi faced a near lockdown situation on Saturday, following a call of protest by Gen Z led Cockroach Janata Party. More than 30,000 security forces were deployed and over 50 metro stations were shut. Authorities imposed an internet blackout for 24 hours to suppress the movement but the protesters managed to slip through the loopholes. FRANCE 24’s team on the ground reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e7c5a9c8-c879-11f1-8c42-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-101905-102106-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e7c5a9c8-c879-11f1-8c42-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-101905-102106-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ed0da94e-c879-11f1-86bf-01cbcb5e47e3</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:03:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Colombians, fearing for future, march against right-wing president</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-colombians-fearing-for-future-march-against-right-wing-president</link><description>
Thousands of Colombians took to the streets of cities across the country on Wednesday to protest the policies of new right-wing President Abelardo de la Espriella. The demonstrations mark the first show of force by the opposition since de la Espriella took office in August vowing to combat crime and eradicate "narco-terrorists." FRANCE 24's Ramón Campos Iriarte reports from Bogotá, Colombia.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3e7298bc-c87a-11f1-85b2-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-102137-102255-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3e7298bc-c87a-11f1-85b2-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-102137-102255-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4395b7ac-c87a-11f1-96e5-d9410d362548</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:00:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Mont Blanc nearly two metres taller than in 2023</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-mont-blanc-nearly-two-metres-taller-than-in-2023</link><description>
France's tallest mountain was nearly two metres higher last month than its last reported measurement in 2023, surveyors said Wednesday, putting the Alpine peak at 4,807.47 metres (15,772.5 feet). Researchers have been measuring the mountain every two years to three years since 2001, hoping to garner information about the impact of climate change on the Alps.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/98abb872-c87a-11f1-a9c0-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-102315-102503-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/98abb872-c87a-11f1-a9c0-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-102315-102503-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9df68834-c87a-11f1-a96f-9bb0f324d8db</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:58:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>PSG outgun embattled Man City in six-goal Champions League thriller</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-psg-outgun-embattled-man-city-in-six-goal-champions-league-thriller</link><description>
Paris Saint-Germain further soured the mood at the Etihad Stadium as Manchester City's first home game since the guilty verdict on widespread flouting of Premier League financial rules ended in a 4-2 Champions League defeat on Wednesday. The European champions turned on the style to strike three times inside the opening 35 minutes through Desire Doue, Ousmane Dembele and Vitinha.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c29a896a-c87a-11f1-abff-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-102530-102704-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c29a896a-c87a-11f1-abff-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-102530-102704-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c76dfe18-c87a-11f1-9b5a-4ff3dd8c3a1f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:57:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Restrictions expose Ukraine's Starlink dependency in Russia war</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-restrictions-expose-ukraine-s-starlink-dependency-in-russia-war</link><description>
Restrictions reported by Ukraine on its use of the US satellite internet system Starlink have exposed Kyiv's reliance on the technology for both offensive and defensive operations in its fight against Russia'a invasion, analysts and observers say. A senior Ukrainian official, who asked not to be named, told AFP on Wednesday that Starlink data communication speeds had been "throttled". The change has come at a time of renewed tension between Kyiv and Washington, with US President Donald Trump seeking to bring down global fuel prices by buying Russian diesel and pressuring both sides to stop attacking energy infrastructure.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/17bfa752-c87d-11f1-bb46-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-103555-103752-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/17bfa752-c87d-11f1-bb46-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-103555-103752-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1c9f3166-c87d-11f1-8c7d-1d14ffb2f6be</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:55:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
